{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1364299-non-passive-uses-of-integrity","id":1364299,"title":"Non-passive uses of Integrity?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-31T01:18:19-08:00","id":1364299,"title":"Non-passive uses of Integrity?","content":"This skill confuses me. I understand it to represent your trained discipline to resist coercion and mental pressure. Sometimes I think I understand it and other times it seems all over the map. It is especially difficult when I've had to explain to players why they should invest their few skill dots in it and wonder what other uses it has or if it is simply a tax to be able to roleplay mentally strong characters or a safeguard in order to not be bullied around, interrogated or mind controlled by NPCs (both of which are rather niche-cases in my games). I now want to know examples of <i>active</i> uses of the skill to allow the players to affect scenes themselves, because a skill that is mainly reactive and passive doesn't sit right with me.<br /> <br /> According to the Trinity books these are active uses of Integrity.<br /> - Lying by hiding your emotions<br /> - Meditating (there is no mention of what this actually does)<br /> <br /> So few potential active uses of a skill is not so satisfactory for me and makes me wonder why it should even be a skill at all at this point apart from the game design principle of never rolling Attribute + Attribute.<br /> <br /> Are these valid examples of non-passive rolls you can do with Integrity?<br /> - General perception rolls, because with higher Integrity you are more focused on details?<br /> - To intimidate, coerce and lead people with your force of will or conviction? (or is this just available through Skill tricks and other extras?)<br /> - Bolster other rolls with Integrity to represent extreme focus? (again, is this only available through extras such as Skill Tricks?)<br /> - Understand the psyche of others, especifically understand if they are headstrong or weak-willed, and knowing how to push them?<br /> <br /> Can you give examples of more uses of this skill other than to just resist coercion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T02:08:27-08:00","id":1364304,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how analogy is similar between games, but reading about Integrity Skills in <b>Storypath</b> I kinda thought about Integrity Trait in <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b>. In <b>CoD</b>, it's trait from 1 to 10 that points how mentally stable character is - if you confront supernatural or leading stressful life, you test Integrity. More you loose of it, more character is suitable for unhinged behavior. Also, she has problems with exorcism of supernatural beings.<br /> <br /> Now, I understand that in <b>Storypath</b>, Integrity being Skill means that you have 'character that are <i>more</i> stable and <i>more</i> hinged in stress' - there is no 'low level' of those concepts. That characters with Integrity Skill are just <i>more</i> stable that rest of general population. But maybe check <b>CoD Rulebook</b>, if you can to compare those concepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T02:26:10-08:00","id":1364306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1364299-non-passive-uses-of-integrity?p=1364304#post1364304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how analogy is similar between games, but reading about Integrity Skills in <b>Storypath</b> I kinda thought about Integrity Trait in <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b>. In <b>CoD</b>, it's trait from 1 to 10 that points how mentally stable character is - if you confront supernatural or leading stressful life, you test Integrity. More you loose of it, more character is suitable for unhinged behavior. Also, she has problems with exorcism of supernatural beings.<br /> <br /> Now, I understand that in <b>Storypath</b>, Integrity being Skill means that you have 'character that are <i>more</i> stable and <i>more</i> hinged in stress' - there is no 'low level' of those concepts. That characters with Integrity Skill are just <i>more</i> stable that rest of general population. But maybe check <b>CoD Rulebook</b>, if you can to compare those concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is a weak analogy because CoD is an entirely different game with different conceits. In CoD Integrity represents the health of your soul when confronted with supernatural and mundane horror. Trinity not being neither a horror game nor dealing with the supernatural or magic does not have such things as health of a soul but rather the level of discipline and strength of will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T11:52:45-08:00","id":1364381,"title":"","content":"Also, Integrity as a Skill has a much more direct place to look in Exalted. Though Exalted would only add actively refuting arguments with your personal principles (that is, rather than engaging in a strictly logical debate on something, making a values based argument) to the list of things to do with it that don't get into Skill Tricks/Edges/etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T12:07:58-08:00","id":1364385,"title":"","content":"Integrity shares a lot of the same space as Sincerity does in L5R. Integrity isn't just about holding on to your personal principles. It's also about appearing to be sincere and truthful. So, yes, lying is a really popular way to use the skill. You could also use it to send a message to your colleague through micro-expressions by maintaining strict control over your facial expressions. You could even use it to appear to by lying while you're telling the truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T12:55:36-08:00","id":1364393,"title":"","content":"And honestly meditation would more likely be Resolve rather then stamina, that is the point and why even elderly can do it. Some uses I would have stamina, but the regularly take half an hour and meditate everyday I would have resolve.<br /> <br /> A lot of the rules are pretty fudgy even without integrity. Sometimes it works good, other times it just seems you can roll any two Skill at Combo for any task if reaaaally want to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T14:08:19-08:00","id":1364403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1364299-non-passive-uses-of-integrity?p=1364393#post1364393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it just seems you can roll any two Skill at Combo for any task if reaaaally want to.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's generally how I run Storypath. It's pretty easy to have basically 5-10 dice every roll. So, I generally use rolls to see how well they succeed rather than if they succeed. (However, I've had plenty of botches at the table, which is its own kind of fun.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T18:01:20-08:00","id":1364443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1364299-non-passive-uses-of-integrity?p=1364393#post1364393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes it works good, other times it just seems you can roll any two Skill at Combo for any task if reaaaally want to.</div> </div> </div> </div>To quote <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/about-the-storypath-system-scion-trinity-continuum.838628/\" target=\"_blank\">Bruce Baugh</a>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Storypath, on the other hand, not only assumes but outright declares that a) you work from the specific to the general and b) discussion with negotiation is how the system works all the time. Your creator of a custom security system starts with Enigmas, or Technology, and then you choose an attribute that expresses the character's approach. Each of the stat categories, or arenas (Mental, Physical, Social), has one stat for the Forceful approach, one for Finesse, and one for Resilience. Intelligence is the Forceful mental attribute: if your character's going this way, they are applying their galaxy brain and familiarity with all Internet traditions to get the job done. Cunning is the Finesse mental attribute: your character is looking for and exploiting loopholes, thinking about the psychology of expected attackers and setting traps for them, and so on. Resolve is the Resilience mental attribute: your character's pressing on with stubborn determination, probably thinking in terms of redundancy and supporting interactions, and like that.<br /> <br /> Robin Laws once remarked that every RPG has a characteristic venue and a characteristic scope of activity within which characters express their identities. In classic Vampire, that's the salon and social competition. In classic D&amp;D it's the dungeon and cunning &amp; fighting. In Feng Shui, it's the fight scene and fighting. Well, Storypath makes <b>every </b>action an expression of character, by the flow of decision from skill to attribute.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> In addition, the game's emphasis on action is supported in the interaction of approach and arena. There are no stats for kinda hanging back and not doing much. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAIBRAA7\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> Your character is always moving forward to engage with the challenge, and it's always a question of how they're doing so. This kind of thing, I've found, shapes play way more than a lot of players ever realize. As Jim Kiley put it in Adventure, &quot;You get what you reward.&quot; Give players an option to be passive and disengaged, and many will take it for fear that an active alternative will turn out be wrong wrong wrong and hurt their character and drag down the group's situation.<br /> <br /> If, on the other hand ... you tell players that all active approaches are good - that every one solves some problems well and makes for entertaining drama in trying to solve ones it's not so great for - the choice moves from &quot;should I risk it?&quot; to &quot;<b>how </b>should I risk it?&quot;, because of course they're taking the kind of risk and get to decide how. Presuming here that players want to have an adventurous good time, the game's stepping up to point out the scenic attractions and give them a hand where the footing's tricky. I love it. </div> </div> </div>tl;dr: that's intentional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T06:07:33-08:00","id":1364525,"title":"","content":"I like the way the \u201csocial skills\u201d work. If you pick Command, Empathy, Integrity and Persuasion, you have a nice combination of skills that have a lot of gray area among them. Even with situations when you have multiple skills to achieve the same result, the same way you can have multiple attributes for the same result, the ones you pick define the way you will deal with the subject.<br /> <br /> For example, you have to convince a guard to leave his spot for some reason. You can lie to him using command, persuasion, integrity or empathy, but the resulting lie is going to be different. Command will be closer to an order (it\u2019s your duty to protect the people in the alley), Persuasion will be a reasonable discussion (you should check that alley there, it is sounding like there is something happening), empathy will grab him by the emotions (I heard some kids screaming about a gun in the alley) and integrity will be a straightforward lie (there is a guy in the alley with a gun).<br /> <br /> tha same happens for crafting technology, you can use Technology, Enigmas and Science, technology is about the hardware, enigmas about software and science about the principles how it works, the results are going to be different? Yes, but for the rules it\u2019s the same, the milestone is done.<br /> <br /> combat is probably the most straightforward skill picking, but you can still work with some variations of athletic feats to hit the target in the lack of proper combat skills, not same results in game, but same rules wise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T13:44:20-08:00","id":1364599,"title":"","content":"The rules don't even need to be exactly the same; especially in one important part: Stunts and Complications. Obviously the rules around those don't change, but which are available/impacting to your character will vary based on what dice-pool you say captures your intent. Breaking down a door, or carefully unlocking it, both get you past the obstacle that is the door. It's not just the descriptive differences though, it's also how those inform the mechanical consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}